    Seed("Dumbbell Lateral Raise", "Stand holding dumbbells at your sides with a slight elbow bend. Raise the arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height, leading with the elbows as if pouring water, then lower slowly. The definitive exercise for the medial deltoids, which create shoulder width. Use strict form and moderate weight.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("traps"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Front Raise", "Stand holding dumbbells in front of the thighs. With straight arms, raise one or both weights forward to shoulder height, then lower under control. Isolates the front deltoids; since these get heavy work from pressing, moderate volume is usually sufficient.", "strength", "shoulders", emptyList(), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Bent-Over Reverse Fly", "Hinge forward until your torso is near parallel, holding dumbbells hanging beneath you with a slight elbow bend. Raise the arms out to the sides, squeezing the shoulder blades, then lower slowly. Targets the rear deltoids and mid-back, essential for balanced shoulder development and posture.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("rhomboids", "traps"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Seated Dumbbell Rear Delt Fly", "Sit on the end of a bench, lean your chest onto your thighs and hold dumbbells beneath your legs. Raise them out to the sides with slightly bent arms, then lower. The seated bent position minimizes momentum for strict rear-delt isolation.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("rhomboids"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Upright Row", "Stand holding dumbbells in front of the thighs and pull them straight up along the body to chest height, elbows leading. Dumbbells let the hands travel freely, making this easier on the wrists and shoulders than the barbell version while training the side delts and traps.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("traps", "biceps"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Cuban Press", "Row light dumbbells up to chest height with elbows bent to 90 degrees, externally rotate the forearms until the weights point upward, then press overhead; reverse the sequence down. A three-phase movement that strengthens the rotator cuff, rear delts and traps, excellent as a warm-up or prehab exercise.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("rotator cuff", "traps"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Shrug-Press Combo (Bradford Press)", "Press a barbell from the front of the shoulders to just over head height, lower it behind the neck, then press back over to the front, alternating continuously without locking out. The constant tension and changing angles burn out all three deltoid heads with light weight.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("triceps", "traps"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Shoulder Press", "Set a seat under the Smith bar so it lowers to chin level. Press the bar overhead along the fixed track and lower with control. The guided path allows safe heavy pressing without a spotter and strict deltoid focus.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("triceps"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Upright Row", "Stand at a Smith machine and pull the bar up the fixed track from thighs to chest height, elbows high. The stable path helps you focus tension on the lateral delts and traps through a strict vertical pull.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("traps", "biceps"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Cable Lateral Raise", "Stand side-on to a low pulley, handle in the far hand. Raise the arm out to the side to shoulder height against the cable, then lower slowly. Unlike dumbbells, the cable provides resistance from the very bottom of the movement, keeping constant tension on the medial deltoid.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("traps"), "cable"),
    Seed("Cable Front Raise", "Stand facing away from a low pulley with the handle in one hand at your thigh. Raise the straight arm forward to shoulder height and lower slowly. The cable's constant tension makes this a strict anterior-deltoid isolation movement.", "strength", "shoulders", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Cable Rear Delt Fly", "Stand centered between two high pulleys, grab the left cable with the right hand and vice versa. Pull the crossed cables out and back until your arms form a T, squeezing the rear delts, then return. Constant cable tension makes this superior for rear-delt isolation.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("rhomboids"), "cable"),
    Seed("Cable Upright Row", "Stand over a low pulley holding a straight bar or rope. Pull it up the front of your body to chest height with elbows leading, then lower. Smooth, constant resistance through the pull trains the side delts and upper traps with less joint stress at the bottom.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("traps", "biceps"), "cable"),
    Seed("Machine Shoulder Press", "Sit in a shoulder press machine with handles at ear level. Press them overhead to full extension and lower under control. The fixed path removes balance demands, making it beginner-friendly and ideal for pushing the deltoids safely to fatigue.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("triceps"), "machine"),
    Seed("Machine Lateral Raise", "Sit in the lateral raise machine with upper arms against the pads. Raise the arms out to shoulder height and lower slowly. The machine locks in perfect raise mechanics, removing the cheating and swinging common with dumbbells.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("traps"), "machine"),
    Seed("Reverse Pec Deck", "Sit facing the pec deck machine with the handles set to the rear-delt position. With slightly bent arms, pull the handles back and out until the arms are in line with the shoulders, squeezing the rear delts and mid-back, then return slowly.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("rhomboids", "traps"), "machine"),
    Seed("Pike Push-Up", "From a push-up position, walk your feet toward your hands and lift the hips high so your torso is near vertical. Bend the elbows to lower the top of your head toward the floor, then press back up. A bodyweight overhead-press substitute that builds serious deltoid and triceps strength.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("triceps", "core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Handstand Push-Up", "Kick up into a handstand against a wall. Lower your head under control toward the floor by bending the elbows, then press back to full lockout. An advanced pressing feat loading the shoulders and triceps with nearly full body weight; master pike push-ups and wall holds first.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("triceps", "core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Wall Walk", "Start in a push-up position with feet against a wall. Walk your feet up the wall while walking your hands back toward it until nearly vertical, then reverse. Builds shoulder strength, stability and the positional confidence needed for handstand work.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("core", "chest"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Overhead Press", "Clean a kettlebell to the rack position at the shoulder, then press it overhead until the arm locks out with the bell resting against the back of the forearm. The offset load challenges shoulder stability through the whole press and strengthens the core against lateral flexion.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("triceps", "core"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Push Press", "From the rack position, dip at the knees and explosively drive the kettlebell overhead using leg drive, catching it at lockout. Lets you overload the shoulders beyond strict-press capability and trains explosive triple extension.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("triceps", "thighs"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Halo", "Hold a kettlebell upside down by the horns at chest height. Circle it slowly around your head, keeping it close, alternating directions. Mobilizes and strengthens the shoulder girdle and thoracic spine while the core resists movement, making it a superb warm-up drill.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("core", "triceps"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Band Pull-Apart", "Hold a resistance band at shoulder height with straight arms and hands shoulder-width apart. Pull the band apart until it touches your chest, squeezing the shoulder blades together, then return slowly. A simple, high-value drill for rear delts, mid-traps and posture; great between pressing sets.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("rhomboids", "traps"), "band"),
    Seed("Front Plate Raise", "Hold a weight plate with both hands at the thighs. With straight arms, raise it to shoulder height or slightly above, pause, and lower slowly. A simple anterior-deltoid builder; raising to eye level and holding briefly adds an isometric challenge.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("core"), "other"),
    Seed("Barbell Curl", "Stand holding a barbell with an underhand, shoulder-width grip at the thighs. Keeping the elbows pinned to your sides, curl the bar up to shoulder height, squeeze, and lower under control to full extension. The classic mass builder for the biceps brachii; avoid swinging the torso or letting the elbows drift forward.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "barbell"),
    Seed("EZ-Bar Curl", "Curl an EZ (cambered) bar using the angled grips, keeping elbows at your sides. The semi-supinated hand position reduces wrist and elbow strain compared with a straight bar while still loading the biceps heavily, making it the go-to curl for many lifters.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Preacher Curl", "Sit at a preacher bench with the backs of your upper arms on the angled pad, holding a barbell or EZ-bar. Curl the bar up, squeeze, and lower to a near-full stretch. The pad eliminates cheating and emphasizes the lower portion of the biceps; never bounce out of the stretched position.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Drag Curl", "Curl a barbell while dragging it up the front of your body, pulling the elbows back behind you rather than keeping them fixed. The bar path removes front-delt assistance and keeps peak tension on the biceps, especially the long head.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Reverse Barbell Curl", "Curl a barbell or EZ-bar with an overhand grip, elbows fixed at the sides. The pronated grip shifts emphasis to the brachialis and brachioradialis of the forearm, building arm thickness and grip strength. Use lighter weight than a standard curl.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Bicep Curl", "Stand with dumbbells at your sides, palms forward. Curl one or both weights to shoulder height while keeping the elbows still, squeeze, and lower fully. Dumbbells allow natural wrist rotation and independent arm work to correct imbalances.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Hammer Curl", "Curl dumbbells with a neutral grip, palms facing each other throughout. The hammer position targets the brachialis and brachioradialis alongside the biceps, adding thickness to the upper arm and forearm and usually permitting heavier loads.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Incline Dumbbell Curl", "Sit back on a 45-60 degree incline bench with arms hanging straight down holding dumbbells. Curl the weights up without letting the elbows drift forward, then lower to a deep stretch. The incline places the biceps long head under stretch, making this one of the best peak-builders.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Concentration Curl", "Sit on a bench, lean forward and brace the back of one upper arm against your inner thigh, dumbbell hanging. Curl the weight to your shoulder with a hard squeeze, then lower slowly. The braced arm eliminates all momentum for maximal biceps isolation.", "strength", "biceps", emptyList(), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Zottman Curl", "Curl dumbbells up with palms facing up, rotate the wrists to a palms-down position at the top, then lower slowly with the overhand grip before rotating back. Combines a standard curl with a reverse eccentric, training the biceps on the way up and the forearms on the way down.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Spider Curl", "Lie chest-down on an incline bench with your arms hanging vertically, holding dumbbells or an EZ-bar. Curl the weight up and squeeze hard at the top, then lower fully. The vertical arm position keeps tension highest in the contracted position, targeting the biceps short head.", "strength", "biceps", emptyList(), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Cable Curl", "Stand facing a low pulley holding a straight or EZ bar attachment. Curl the bar to your shoulders with elbows pinned, then lower under control. The cable maintains tension through the entire range, including at the bottom where dumbbells go slack.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "cable"),
    Seed("Cable Rope Hammer Curl", "Attach a rope to a low pulley and curl it up with a neutral grip, keeping elbows at your sides and squeezing at the top. Combines constant cable tension with the brachialis emphasis of the hammer grip.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "cable"),
    Seed("High Cable Curl", "Stand between two high pulleys, arms out to the sides holding the handles. Curl the handles toward your ears in a double biceps pose motion, squeezing hard, then extend. Trains the biceps in a shortened, flexed-shoulder position and delivers an intense peak contraction.", "strength", "biceps", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Machine Preacher Curl", "Sit at the curl machine with upper arms on the pad and grip the handles. Curl through the machine's arc, squeeze, and lower to a controlled stretch. The fixed path keeps tension consistent and safe, ideal for drop sets and training to failure.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "machine"),
    Seed("Chin-Up (Biceps Focus)", "Perform chin-ups with a narrow underhand grip, deliberately initiating the pull by flexing the elbows and keeping the torso vertical. Loaded with body weight, this is one of the heaviest biceps stimuli available, while the lats assist.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("lats", "forearms"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Resistance Band Curl", "Stand on a resistance band and curl the handles up with elbows fixed at your sides. Band tension increases toward the top, matching the biceps strength curve. Convenient for home workouts, warm-ups and high-repetition pump work.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "band"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Curl", "Curl a kettlebell held by the horns or by the handle with a neutral grip. The bell's offset center of mass increases the challenge at the top of the curl and works the grip and forearms harder than a comparable dumbbell.", "strength", "biceps", listOf("forearms"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Skull Crusher", "Lie on a flat bench holding an EZ-bar or barbell over your chest with a narrow grip. Keeping the upper arms vertical and still, bend the elbows to lower the bar to your forehead or just behind the head, then extend back to lockout. A premier mass builder for all three triceps heads; lower slowly and never bounce.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "barbell"),
    Seed("Incline Skull Crusher", "Perform skull crushers on a slight incline bench, lowering the bar behind the head. The incline increases the stretch on the triceps long head, enhancing its growth stimulus. Keep the elbows narrow and the movement strict.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "barbell"),
    Seed("JM Press", "A hybrid between a close-grip bench press and a skull crusher: lower the bar toward the chin/upper chest with elbows tucked and forearms folding onto the biceps, then press back to lockout. Popular among powerlifters for building lockout strength.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest", "shoulders"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Lying Dumbbell Triceps Extension", "Lie on a bench holding dumbbells above your chest with neutral grips. Keeping the upper arms fixed, bend the elbows to lower the weights beside your head, then extend back up. Dumbbells allow a natural wrist position and independent arm work.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Overhead Dumbbell Triceps Extension", "Seated or standing, hold one dumbbell with both hands overhead. Lower it behind your head by bending the elbows, keeping them pointed forward, then extend to lockout. The overhead position fully stretches the long head of the triceps, the muscle's largest portion.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("core"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Kickback", "Hinge forward with a flat back, upper arm parallel to the floor and elbow bent holding a dumbbell. Extend the forearm back until the arm is straight, squeeze, and return. Peak tension occurs at full contraction, making kickbacks a great finishing and mind-muscle exercise.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("rear delts"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Tate Press", "Lie on a bench holding dumbbells over your chest with palms facing your feet. Bend the elbows outward to lower the dumbbells to your chest so they point at each other, then extend back up. An elbow-friendly extension favored by bench-press specialists.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Cable Triceps Pushdown", "Stand facing a high pulley with a straight bar or V-bar. With elbows pinned to your sides, push the bar down until the arms fully extend, squeeze, and let it rise to about chest height. The most popular triceps isolation exercise, with smooth constant tension and easy load adjustment.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Rope Pushdown", "Perform a pushdown using a rope attachment, spreading the rope ends apart at the bottom of each rep. The neutral grip and outward spread increase activation of the lateral triceps head and allow a stronger peak contraction.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Overhead Cable Triceps Extension", "Face away from a high or mid pulley holding a rope overhead, elbows bent behind your head. Extend the arms forward and up to lockout, then return to a deep stretch. Combines the long-head stretch of overhead work with the cable's constant tension.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("core"), "cable"),
    Seed("Single-Arm Reverse-Grip Pushdown", "Grip a single handle on a high pulley with an underhand grip and press it down to full extension with the elbow pinned. The supinated grip biases the medial head of the triceps and lets each arm work independently.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Bench Dip", "Sit on the edge of a bench, hands beside your hips, and walk your feet forward so your hips clear the bench. Lower your body by bending the elbows to about 90 degrees, then press back up. Elevate the feet or add a plate on the lap to progress. Keep the shoulders down and avoid excessive depth.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest", "shoulders"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Triceps Dip", "On parallel bars, keep the torso upright and elbows tucked as you lower until the upper arms are parallel to the floor, then press to lockout. The vertical torso biases the triceps over the chest; add weight with a belt once bodyweight sets exceed ten reps.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest", "shoulders"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Close-Grip Push-Up", "Perform push-ups with hands directly under the shoulders or closer, elbows brushing the ribs as you lower. The narrow hand position shifts the workload strongly onto the triceps while still training the chest and core.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest", "core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Bodyweight Triceps Extension", "Set a bar in a rack at waist height. Grip it in a straight-arm plank position, then bend only the elbows to lower your head under the bar, and extend back up. Difficulty scales with bar height, providing a joint-friendly skull-crusher alternative loaded with body weight.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("core", "shoulders"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Machine Triceps Extension", "Sit at the triceps extension machine with upper arms on the pad and grip the handles. Extend the arms to lockout, squeeze, and return under control. The fixed path isolates the triceps safely and suits drop sets and high-rep finishing work.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Machine Dip", "Sit at a seated dip machine and press the handles down until the arms extend, then return with control. Replicates the dip pattern with adjustable load, letting beginners build pressing strength and advanced lifters overload beyond body weight.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest", "shoulders"), "machine"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Close-Grip Bench Press", "Perform a close-grip bench press under the Smith machine, lowering the bar to the lower chest with elbows tucked and pressing to lockout. The fixed track lets you push the triceps hard without balance concerns or a spotter.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest", "shoulders"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Band Triceps Pushdown", "Anchor a resistance band overhead, grip the ends and push down to full elbow extension with elbows pinned to your sides. Band tension peaks at lockout where the triceps are strongest. A convenient warm-up, home-training and finishing movement.", "strength", "triceps", emptyList(), "band"),
    Seed("Diamond Knee Push-Up", "Perform a diamond push-up from the knees, hands close together beneath the chest. A regression that lets beginners develop the triceps and chest strength required for full close-grip push-ups while keeping strict elbow-tucked form.", "strength", "triceps", listOf("chest"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Barbell Back Squat", "Rest a barbell across your upper traps, feet shoulder-width apart with toes slightly out. Brace the core, sit the hips down and back while the knees track over the toes, descending until the thighs reach at least parallel, then drive up through the whole foot to standing. The foundational lower-body lift, building the quads, glutes, hamstrings and trunk. Keep the chest up and heels planted throughout.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings", "calves", "core"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Front Squat", "Hold the barbell across the front of the shoulders in a clean grip or with crossed arms, elbows high. Squat down keeping the torso as upright as possible, then drive back up. The front-loaded position shifts emphasis to the quads and demands strong upper-back and core engagement; it is also more knee-dominant and lower-back friendly.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Box Squat", "Squat down to a box set at or slightly below parallel, sit back fully onto it while staying tight, pause briefly, and drive back up. Sitting back to the box builds hip strength, teaches depth consistency and reduces knee strain; popular among powerlifters for developing explosive strength out of the hole.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Pause Squat", "Perform a back or front squat with a deliberate two-to-three-second pause at the bottom before driving up. Removing the stretch reflex forces pure strength from the deepest position, building bottom-end power and rock-solid positional control.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Zercher Squat", "Cradle a barbell in the crooks of your elbows against the torso, then squat. The front-loaded carry position hammers the quads, upper back and core, and the natural upright torso makes it useful for lifters with limited mobility. Wrap the bar with a pad for comfort.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core", "biceps"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Lunge", "With a barbell on your upper back, step forward into a lunge, lowering the rear knee toward the floor while the front shin stays near vertical, then push back to standing. Trains each leg independently, developing quad and glute strength, balance and hip stability.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings", "calves"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Reverse Lunge", "With a barbell on the back, step backward into a lunge, lowering the rear knee toward the floor, then drive off the front leg to return. Reverse lunges are more knee-friendly than forward lunges and place greater emphasis on the glutes of the front leg.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Walking Lunge", "With a barbell across your back, lunge forward and, instead of returning, bring the rear foot through into the next lunge, walking continuously. The alternating pattern adds a balance and conditioning element, torching the quads and glutes over distance.", "reps_distance", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings", "calves", "core"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Bulgarian Split Squat", "Place your rear foot on a bench behind you with a barbell on your back and the front foot forward. Lower straight down until the front thigh is near parallel, then drive up. One of the most effective unilateral leg builders, loading the front-leg quad and glute intensely while training balance.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Step-Up", "With a barbell on your back, place one foot fully on a knee-height box. Drive through that heel to step up until standing on the box, then lower under control. Minimize push-off from the trailing leg to keep the work on the lead-leg quad and glute.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Hack Squat", "Stand with a barbell behind your legs at arm's length. Squat down to grip it, then stand up, dragging the bar up the back of the legs. An old-school quad builder that keeps the torso upright; the modern machine hack squat evolved from this movement.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "forearms"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Overhead Squat", "Hold a barbell locked out overhead with a wide snatch grip and squat to full depth while keeping the bar over the middle of the foot. Demands exceptional mobility, balance and trunk strength; a cornerstone of Olympic weightlifting preparation. Start with an empty bar or PVC pipe.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("shoulders", "core", "glutes"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Goblet Squat", "Hold a dumbbell or kettlebell vertically against your chest with both hands. Squat down between your knees to full depth, keeping the torso upright and elbows inside the knees, then stand. The front load counterbalances the hips, making it the best squat-teaching tool and a legitimate quad builder.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Lunge", "Hold dumbbells at your sides and step forward into a lunge, lowering the rear knee toward the floor, then push back to standing. The dumbbells add load without a bar on the spine, also challenging grip and posture over a set.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings", "forearms"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Bulgarian Split Squat", "With the rear foot elevated on a bench and dumbbells at your sides, lower into a deep single-leg squat and drive back up. The dumbbell version is easier to set up and bail from than the barbell variation, making it the most popular way to load this brutal unilateral movement.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Step-Up", "Holding dumbbells at your sides, step onto a knee-height box, driving through the lead heel to stand tall, then lower slowly. Builds single-leg strength, balance and hip stability with minimal spinal loading; control the descent rather than dropping.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Squat", "Stand holding heavy dumbbells at your sides and squat until the thighs reach parallel, keeping the chest up, then stand. A simple, accessible squat pattern; grip usually fatigues before the legs, so use straps or switch to goblet position for lighter bells.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "forearms"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Sissy Squat Hybrid (Cyclist Squat)", "Elevate your heels on a wedge or plates, hold a dumbbell at the chest and squat with an upright torso, letting the knees travel far forward. The heel elevation maximizes knee flexion and quad stretch, delivering an intense stimulus to the quadriceps, especially the rectus femoris.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Squat", "Position yourself under the Smith bar and squat along the fixed vertical track, feet slightly in front of the bar. The guided path removes balance demands, allowing pure focus on leg drive and making it safer to squat heavy without a spotter, though it trains fewer stabilizers than a free squat.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Split Squat", "Perform a split squat or Bulgarian split squat under the Smith machine bar. The fixed track stabilizes the load so you can concentrate entirely on driving through the front leg, making it excellent for strict unilateral quad and glute overload.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Front Squat", "Rest the Smith bar across the front of your shoulders and squat along the fixed track with an upright torso. Provides the quad emphasis of a front squat without requiring the wrist mobility or balance of the barbell version.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Leg Press", "Sit in the leg press with feet shoulder-width on the platform. Lower the sled until the knees approach the chest without the lower back rounding off the pad, then press back up without locking the knees hard. Allows very heavy quad and glute loading with minimal spinal compression and balance demands.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "machine"),
    Seed("Single-Leg Press", "Perform the leg press one leg at a time with the foot centered on the platform. Corrects side-to-side strength imbalances and increases range of motion; use notably less than half your two-leg weight to start.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "machine"),
    Seed("Hack Squat Machine", "Position your shoulders under the pads of the hack squat sled with your back flat against the pad. Squat deep along the machine's track and drive back up. The supported back and fixed angle allow aggressive quad loading through a long range of motion.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes"), "machine"),
    Seed("Leg Extension", "Sit in the leg extension machine with the pad on your lower shins. Extend the knees until the legs are straight, squeeze the quads hard at the top, and lower under control. The only true isolation exercise for all four quadriceps heads; use controlled tempo rather than momentum.", "strength", "thighs", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Belt Squat", "Stand on a belt squat platform with the load hanging from a hip belt and squat to depth. Loads the legs heavily with zero spinal compression, making it invaluable for lifters with back issues or during heavy training phases.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "machine"),
    Seed("Machine Sissy Squat", "Lock your calves and feet into a sissy squat bench, then lean back and lower your torso and thighs as one line by bending only at the knees, then pull back up with the quads. Produces an extreme quad stretch and contraction; scale depth gradually.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("core"), "machine"),
    Seed("Bodyweight Squat", "Stand with feet shoulder-width apart and squat until the thighs reach at least parallel, arms reaching forward for balance, then stand. The foundational human movement pattern; perfect for warm-ups, high-rep conditioning and learning squat mechanics before loading.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Jump Squat", "Descend into a quarter-to-half squat and explode upward into a vertical jump, landing softly with bent knees directly into the next rep. Develops lower-body power and rate of force development; keep landings quiet and controlled.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Pistol Squat", "Stand on one leg with the other extended straight in front of you, then squat all the way down on the standing leg and drive back up. An elite single-leg strength and mobility feat; progress using a box, counterweight or assistance from a strap.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core", "calves"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Walking Lunge", "Lunge forward, lower the rear knee toward the floor, then bring the back foot through into the next stride, walking continuously. A high-value bodyweight movement for leg strength, hip mobility and conditioning; add distance or speed to progress.", "reps_distance", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings", "calves"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Split Squat", "Take a staggered stance and lower straight down until the rear knee nearly touches the floor, keeping the front shin near vertical, then drive up without moving the feet. The static base makes it the ideal entry point into single-leg training.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Wall Sit", "Slide your back down a wall until your hips and knees form 90-degree angles, thighs parallel to the floor, and hold. An isometric quad endurance builder useful for beginners, rehab and skiers; accumulate time or add a plate on the thighs to progress.", "duration", "thighs", listOf("glutes"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Sissy Squat", "Rise onto the balls of your feet, hold a support, and lean your torso back while driving the knees forward and down toward the floor, keeping hips extended, then pull back up with the quads. An old-school movement giving an unmatched stretch to the rectus femoris.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Step-Up", "Step onto a sturdy box or bench with one foot, driving through the heel to stand tall on top, then step down under control. Simple, scalable single-leg work; increase box height or hold weight to progress.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Goblet Squat", "Hold a kettlebell by the horns against your chest and squat to full depth with an upright torso, elbows tracking inside the knees, then stand tall. The kettlebell's compact shape makes it the ideal goblet-squat implement for teaching depth and posture.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Front Rack Squat", "Clean one or two kettlebells to the rack position at the shoulders and squat to depth while keeping the torso vertical. The rack position challenges the core and upper back isometrically while the legs drive the movement.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Lunge Pass-Through", "Perform alternating lunges while passing a kettlebell under the front leg from hand to hand at the bottom of each rep. Adds coordination, grip and core anti-rotation work to the standard lunge pattern.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core", "forearms"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Cable Squat", "Face a low pulley holding the handles or a bar, lean back slightly against the cable tension and squat deep, then stand. The forward-pulling cable counterbalances your hips, allowing a very upright, quad-dominant squat that is easy on the lower back.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes"), "cable"),
    Seed("Sled Push", "Load a prowler sled, grip the poles with arms extended and drive it forward with powerful alternating leg strides, staying low. Builds leg strength, power and brutal conditioning with no eccentric loading, so soreness stays low even after hard sessions.", "distance", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves", "core"), "other"),
    Seed("Stiff-Leg Deadlift", "Hold a barbell at the thighs and, with knees nearly straight, hinge at the hips to lower the bar down the legs until a deep hamstring stretch is reached, then extend the hips to stand. Similar to a Romanian deadlift but with straighter knees and often a slightly greater range, maximizing the hamstring stretch. Keep the back flat at all times.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("glutes", "back"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Hip Thrust", "Sit with your upper back against a bench and a padded barbell over your hips, feet flat and knees bent. Drive the hips upward until the torso and thighs form a straight line, squeezing the glutes hard at the top with a posterior pelvic tilt, then lower. The most direct heavy loading available for the gluteus maximus.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings", "thighs"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Glute Bridge", "Lie on the floor with a padded barbell across your hips, knees bent and feet flat. Drive the hips up until fully extended, squeeze the glutes, and lower. The floor version of the hip thrust with a shorter range, ideal for beginners and for very heavy overload.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Deficit Deadlift", "Stand on a low platform or plate so the bar starts below normal height, then perform a deadlift. The increased range of motion demands greater hamstring and hip flexibility and builds strength off the floor. Use lighter loads than a standard deadlift.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("glutes", "back", "thighs"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Snatch-Grip Deadlift", "Deadlift with a very wide snatch grip, which forces a lower hip position and longer pull. Dramatically increases the demand on the hamstrings, upper back and traps. A favorite of Olympic lifters and a brutal posterior-chain builder.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("glutes", "back", "traps"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Single-Leg Romanian Deadlift", "Stand on one leg holding a dumbbell or kettlebell. Hinge forward, extending the free leg straight behind you as a counterbalance, lowering the weight toward the floor with a flat back, then return to standing. Builds hamstring and glute strength alongside balance and hip stability.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("glutes", "core"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift", "Hold dumbbells in front of your thighs and hinge at the hips with soft knees, sliding the weights down the legs until a strong hamstring stretch, then drive the hips forward to stand. A convenient RDL variation with a natural grip and easy setup.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("glutes", "back", "forearms"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Nordic Hamstring Curl", "Kneel with your ankles anchored under a pad or held by a partner. Keeping hips extended, lower your torso toward the floor as slowly as possible using the hamstrings, catch yourself with your hands, and push back or curl up. Elite eccentric hamstring strength work proven to reduce hamstring injury risk.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("calves", "glutes"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Glute Ham Raise", "On a GHD machine with feet secured and thighs on the pad, lower the torso from vertical toward horizontal, then curl the body back up by flexing the knees and extending the hips. Trains the hamstrings at both the hip and knee simultaneously, a rare and valuable stimulus.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("glutes", "calves", "back"), "machine"),
    Seed("Lying Leg Curl", "Lie face down on the leg curl machine with the pad above your heels. Curl your heels toward your glutes, squeeze, and lower slowly to full extension. Directly isolates the hamstrings through knee flexion; avoid lifting the hips off the pad.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("calves"), "machine"),
    Seed("Seated Leg Curl", "Sit in the machine with the pad on the back of the ankles and thighs secured. Curl the legs down and back as far as possible, then return slowly. Research suggests the seated position, which stretches the hamstrings at the hip, produces superior hamstring growth compared with lying curls.", "strength", "hamstrings", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Standing Single-Leg Curl", "Stand at the machine and curl one heel toward your glutes against the pad, squeezing at the top. Unilateral knee flexion work that evens out left-right imbalances and provides a strong peak contraction.", "strength", "hamstrings", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Cable Pull-Through", "Face away from a low pulley with a rope between your legs. Hinge at the hips letting the rope pull back through, then snap the hips forward to stand tall, squeezing the glutes. Teaches the hip hinge with constant tension and minimal spinal load; ideal preparation for deadlifts and swings.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings"), "cable"),
    Seed("Cable Kickback", "Attach an ankle cuff to a low cable, face the stack, and drive one leg straight back and slightly up, squeezing the glute at full hip extension before returning. Isolates the gluteus maximus one side at a time; keep the torso still and avoid arching the lower back.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings"), "cable"),
    Seed("Cable Hip Abduction", "With an ankle cuff on a low cable, stand side-on to the stack and raise the outer leg directly out to the side against resistance, then return. Targets the gluteus medius and minimus, key muscles for hip stability and knee tracking.", "strength", "glutes", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Hip Abduction Machine", "Sit in the abduction machine with the pads against your outer thighs and press the legs apart against resistance, then return slowly. Strengthens the gluteus medius and minimus, improving hip stability, aesthetics and knee health.", "strength", "glutes", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Hip Adduction Machine", "Sit in the adduction machine with pads against your inner thighs, legs apart, and squeeze the legs together, then return with control. Strengthens the adductor group, important for squat depth, sprinting and groin injury prevention.", "strength", "thighs", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Swing", "Hinge at the hips and hike a kettlebell back between your legs, then snap the hips forward explosively so the bell floats to chest height with arms relaxed, letting it swing back into the next rep. The signature kettlebell movement, building explosive hip power, posterior-chain strength and conditioning. Power comes from the hips, never the arms.", "reps_duration", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings", "back", "core"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Single-Leg Glute Bridge", "Lie on your back with one knee bent and the other leg extended. Drive through the planted heel to lift the hips until fully extended, squeezing the glute, then lower. A simple unilateral glute builder that exposes and corrects side-to-side differences.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings", "core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Frog Pump", "Lie on your back with the soles of your feet together and knees dropped out to the sides. Drive the hips up by squeezing the glutes, pause at the top, and lower. The externally rotated position minimizes hamstring involvement, making it a pure high-rep glute pump exercise.", "strength", "glutes", emptyList(), "body weight"),
    Seed("Reverse Hyperextension", "Lie face down on a reverse hyper machine with your legs hanging and hips at the pad's edge. Swing or raise the legs up behind you until level with the torso, squeezing the glutes, then lower. Strengthens the glutes and spinal erectors while gently decompressing the lower back.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings", "back"), "machine"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Hip Thrust", "Set up a hip thrust with your upper back on a bench and the padded Smith bar across your hips. Drive the hips to full extension along the fixed track and lower with control. The guided bar simplifies setup and balance, letting you focus entirely on glute drive.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Donkey Kick", "On all fours with a flat back, drive one bent leg up and back until the sole of the foot faces the ceiling and the thigh is in line with the torso, squeezing the glute, then return. A beginner-friendly glute activation drill; add a band or ankle weight to progress.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Fire Hydrant", "From all fours, lift one bent knee out to the side as high as possible without rotating the torso, then lower. Targets the gluteus medius and hip external rotators, improving hip stability and warming up the hips before squats.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Standing Calf Raise", "Stand in the calf raise machine with shoulders under the pads and the balls of your feet on the platform, heels hanging. Lower the heels to a deep stretch, then rise as high as possible onto the toes, pausing at the top. Trains the gastrocnemius with the knees straight; use full range and controlled tempo.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Seated Calf Raise", "Sit at the seated calf machine with the pads on your knees and the balls of your feet on the platform. Lower the heels to a full stretch, then press up onto the toes. The bent-knee position shifts emphasis to the soleus, the deep calf muscle responsible for much of lower-leg size.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Barbell Standing Calf Raise", "With a barbell across your upper back, stand with the balls of your feet on a plate or block. Rise onto the toes as high as possible, pause, and lower to a stretch. A simple heavy calf option in any rack; balance carefully or perform inside the rack with safeties.", "strength", "calves", listOf("core"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Single-Leg Calf Raise", "Stand on one foot on a step holding a dumbbell on the same side, heel hanging off the edge. Lower into a deep stretch and rise fully onto the toes. Unilateral loading doubles the stimulus per leg and fixes imbalances; hold a support with the free hand.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Calf Raise", "Stand under the Smith bar with the balls of your feet on a block. Rise onto your toes against the fixed bar and lower to a deep stretch. The guided path removes balance demands so you can load heavy and focus on a full range of motion.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Leg Press Calf Raise", "Sit in the leg press and place the balls of your feet at the bottom edge of the platform, legs extended. Press the platform away by pointing the toes, then let the heels come back for a deep stretch. Allows heavy, safe calf loading with no balance requirement.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Donkey Calf Raise", "Bend forward at the hips with your torso supported, load resting over the hips, and the balls of the feet on a block. Rise onto the toes and lower slowly. The stretched hip position lengthens the gastrocnemius, making this old-school movement exceptionally effective.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Bodyweight Calf Raise", "Stand with the balls of your feet on a step, heels hanging. Rise as high as possible onto the toes, pause, then lower until a deep stretch is felt. Simple and effective anywhere; progress with single-leg versions, slow tempos and high volume.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "body weight"),
    Seed("Tibialis Raise", "Lean your back against a wall with feet a step away. Keeping heels planted, lift the toes and balls of both feet toward your shins as high as possible, then lower. Strengthens the tibialis anterior, balancing the calves, protecting the shins and improving ankle resilience.", "strength", "calves", emptyList(), "body weight"),
    Seed("Barbell Wrist Curl", "Sit with your forearms resting on your thighs or a bench, palms up, holding a barbell with wrists hanging off the edge. Curl the wrists upward, squeezing the forearm flexors, then lower to a full stretch. Builds the inner forearm and grip strength; use light weight and high reps.", "strength", "forearms", emptyList(), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Reverse Wrist Curl", "With forearms supported and palms facing down, raise the backs of your hands upward against the barbell, then lower slowly. Strengthens the wrist extensors on top of the forearm, balancing flexor work and protecting the elbows from conditions like tennis elbow.", "strength", "forearms", emptyList(), "barbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Wrist Curl", "Rest one forearm on a bench, palm up, holding a dumbbell with the wrist off the edge. Curl the wrist up and lower to a deep stretch. Working one arm at a time allows a comfortable natural wrist path and balanced forearm flexor development.", "strength", "forearms", emptyList(), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Farmer's Walk", "Pick up a heavy dumbbell or farmer handle in each hand and walk with tall posture, braced core and controlled steps for a set distance or time. The simplest total-body strength exercise there is, building crushing grip, trap and core strength and real-world carrying capacity.", "distance", "forearms", listOf("traps", "core", "calves"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Suitcase Carry", "Carry a single heavy kettlebell or dumbbell at one side and walk tall without leaning toward or away from the load. The offset weight forces the obliques and QL to stabilize the spine, building grip and lateral core strength simultaneously.", "distance", "forearms", listOf("core", "traps"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Plate Pinch", "Pinch two smooth weight plates together between your fingers and thumb and hold for time or carry for distance. Directly trains thumb and pinch-grip strength, an aspect of grip barely touched by normal lifting.", "duration", "forearms", emptyList(), "other"),
    Seed("Wrist Roller", "Hold a wrist roller device with arms extended and roll a hanging weight up by rotating the handle hand-over-hand, then lower it back down under control. One of the most intense forearm burners available, hitting the flexors and extensors in one continuous set.", "strength", "forearms", listOf("shoulders"), "other"),
    Seed("Dead Hang", "Hang from a pull-up bar with straight arms and relaxed shoulders or an active shoulder pack, holding for time. Builds grip endurance, decompresses the spine and improves shoulder health; a foundational step toward pull-ups.", "duration", "forearms", listOf("lats", "shoulders"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Cable Wrist Curl", "Kneel or sit facing a low pulley with forearms braced, holding a straight bar palms up. Curl the wrists against the constant cable tension and lower to a stretch. The smooth resistance keeps tension on the forearm flexors throughout the entire range.", "strength", "forearms", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Plank", "Support yourself on your forearms and toes with the body forming a rigid straight line from head to heels. Brace the abs, squeeze the glutes and breathe steadily while holding the position for time. The foundational anti-extension core exercise; quality of tension matters more than duration.", "duration", "core", listOf("shoulders", "glutes"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Side Plank", "Lie on your side and prop yourself up on one forearm with feet stacked, lifting the hips so the body forms a straight line. Hold, keeping the top shoulder and hip stacked. Trains the obliques and quadratus lumborum against lateral flexion, key for spinal stability.", "duration", "core", listOf("shoulders", "glutes"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Crunch", "Lie on your back with knees bent and feet flat. Curl your shoulders and upper back off the floor by contracting the abs, exhaling as you rise, then lower slowly. A simple rectus abdominis isolation movement; avoid pulling on the neck and focus on spinal flexion rather than height.", "strength", "core", emptyList(), "body weight"),
    Seed("Bicycle Crunch", "Lie on your back with hands lightly behind your head and legs raised. Alternately bring each elbow toward the opposite knee while extending the other leg, pedaling continuously. Combines trunk flexion with rotation, strongly recruiting the obliques and rectus abdominis.", "strength", "core", emptyList(), "body weight"),
    Seed("Reverse Crunch", "Lie on your back with knees bent above the hips. Curl the pelvis up off the floor, bringing the knees toward the chest using the lower abs, then lower slowly without arching the back. Emphasizes the often-neglected lower portion of the rectus abdominis.", "strength", "core", emptyList(), "body weight"),
    Seed("Sit-Up", "Lie on your back with knees bent and rise all the way up to a seated position by flexing the trunk, then lower under control. Works the abs through a long range with significant hip-flexor assistance; anchor the feet only if needed and keep the movement smooth.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("V-Up", "Lie flat with arms extended overhead. Simultaneously raise your straight legs and torso, reaching your hands toward your toes so the body forms a V, then lower with control. An advanced movement demanding strong abs, hip flexors and coordination.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Hollow Body Hold", "Lie on your back and press the lower back into the floor while raising the shoulders, arms and straight legs off the ground, forming a shallow dish shape. Hold while breathing. A gymnastics staple that builds total-body tension and deep core strength transferring to nearly every lift.", "duration", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Leg Raise", "Lie flat with legs straight and hands under the hips or at the sides. Raise the legs to vertical while keeping the lower back pressed down, then lower slowly without letting the back arch. Targets the lower abs and hip flexors; bend the knees to regress.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Hanging Knee Raise", "Hang from a pull-up bar and raise your knees toward your chest, curling the pelvis at the top, then lower under control without swinging. Builds the lower abs and grip; the strict pelvic curl is what separates ab work from mere hip flexion.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors", "forearms"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Hanging Leg Raise", "Hang from a bar and raise straight legs until they are at least parallel to the floor, ideally to the bar, curling the pelvis upward, then lower slowly. One of the hardest and most productive ab exercises, demanding strength, control and grip endurance.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors", "forearms"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Toes-to-Bar", "Hang from a pull-up bar and raise your legs until the toes touch the bar, using a controlled or rhythmic kipping style, then lower. A CrossFit staple combining extreme hip flexion with lat and grip engagement.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors", "lats", "forearms"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Mountain Climber", "From a push-up position, drive one knee toward the chest, then rapidly switch legs in a running motion while keeping the hips low and core braced. Trains core stability and hip flexor speed while doubling as intense cardiovascular conditioning.", "reps_duration", "core", listOf("shoulders", "hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Dead Bug", "Lie on your back with arms pointing at the ceiling and knees bent at 90 degrees over the hips. Slowly extend one arm overhead and the opposite leg toward the floor while the lower back stays pressed down, then return and switch sides. Teaches core bracing under limb movement, superb for beginners and back health.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Bird Dog", "From all fours with a flat back, extend one arm forward and the opposite leg back until both are level with the torso, pause without twisting, then switch. Builds anti-rotation stability and coordination between the core, glutes and spinal erectors.", "strength", "core", listOf("glutes", "back"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Russian Twist", "Sit with knees bent and torso leaned back to about 45 degrees, feet on or off the floor. Rotate the torso side to side, touching the hands or a weight to the floor beside each hip. Trains rotational strength through the obliques; move from the trunk, not the arms.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Flutter Kick", "Lie on your back with legs extended and slightly raised, lower back pressed down. Kick the legs up and down in small rapid alternating movements. An endurance burner for the lower abs and hip flexors used heavily in military-style training.", "duration", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Ab Wheel Rollout", "Kneel holding an ab wheel beneath your shoulders. Roll the wheel forward, extending your body toward the floor while keeping the abs braced and back flat, then pull back to the start using the abs and lats. One of the most potent anti-extension core exercises; only roll as far as you can control.", "strength", "core", listOf("lats", "shoulders"), "other"),
    Seed("Barbell Rollout", "Kneel behind a loaded barbell, grip it shoulder-width and roll it forward until the body approaches full extension, then contract the abs to pull back. Identical in effect to the ab wheel with a scalable, stable implement available in any gym.", "strength", "core", listOf("lats", "shoulders"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Landmine Rotation", "Hold the end of a landmine barbell at arm's length in front of you and sweep it in an arc from hip to hip, rotating through the torso while the arms stay long. Builds rotational power through the obliques with smooth, controlled resistance.", "strength", "core", listOf("shoulders"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Weighted Sit-Up", "Perform a sit-up while hugging a weight plate or dumbbell to your chest, or holding it overhead for greater difficulty. Adds progressive overload to trunk flexion so the abs can grow stronger like any other muscle.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "other"),
    Seed("Cable Crunch", "Kneel below a high pulley holding a rope beside your head. Crunch your torso down, driving the elbows toward the thighs by flexing the spine, then return under control. The standing stack allows heavy, progressive loading of the rectus abdominis, making it the top choice for building visible ab thickness.", "strength", "core", emptyList(), "cable"),
    Seed("Cable Woodchopper", "Stand side-on to a high pulley, grip the handle with both hands and pull it diagonally across the body from high to low, rotating through the hips and trunk, then return. Trains rotational power in the pattern used in sport, golf and throwing.", "strength", "core", listOf("shoulders", "obliques"), "cable"),
    Seed("Low-to-High Cable Chop", "Set the pulley low, grip the handle with both hands by one hip and drive it diagonally up across the body to the opposite shoulder, rotating the trunk. The upward chop pattern builds obliques and hip-to-shoulder power transfer.", "strength", "core", listOf("shoulders"), "cable"),
    Seed("Pallof Press", "Stand side-on to a cable at chest height, holding the handle at your sternum with both hands. Press the handle straight out and hold as the cable tries to rotate you, then return. The definitive anti-rotation exercise, teaching the core to resist twisting forces that cause injury.", "strength", "core", listOf("shoulders"), "cable"),
    Seed("Ab Crunch Machine", "Sit in the ab machine with the pads on your chest or shoulders and crunch forward against the resistance, flexing the spine, then return slowly. Provides easily adjustable progressive overload for the abs with a fixed, safe movement path.", "strength", "core", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Torso Rotation Machine", "Sit in the rotary torso machine, brace the pads and rotate your trunk against resistance to one side, return, and repeat both directions. Isolates the obliques through controlled rotation; use moderate range and avoid jerky end-range twisting.", "strength", "core", emptyList(), "machine"),
    Seed("Roman Chair Sit-Up", "Sit on a Roman chair or GHD with feet anchored and thighs supported. Lower the torso back below parallel, then sit up by flexing the trunk and hips. Extends the sit-up range of motion; build up gradually as the stretched position is demanding.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "machine"),
    Seed("Decline Sit-Up", "Hook your feet into a decline bench and perform sit-ups against the incline, optionally holding a plate. The decline increases the resistance through the whole range, letting you progressively overload trunk flexion.", "strength", "core", listOf("hip flexors"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Dragon Flag", "Lie on a bench gripping it behind your head. Raise your entire body to vertical resting on the upper back, then lower it as one rigid line toward the bench without breaking at the hips. Popularized by Bruce Lee, an elite anti-extension feat; progress with bent knees or partial lowering.", "strength", "core", listOf("lats", "glutes"), "body weight"),
    Seed("L-Sit", "Support yourself on parallettes, dip bars or the floor with straight arms, and hold your legs extended straight out in front, parallel to the ground. A gymnastics isometric demanding severe core, hip flexor and triceps strength; tuck the knees to regress.", "duration", "core", listOf("hip flexors", "triceps", "shoulders"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Suitcase Deadlift", "Deadlift a single heavy kettlebell or dumbbell positioned beside one leg, keeping the shoulders and hips perfectly level against the offset load. Trains the lateral core hard while grooving the deadlift pattern; an underrated anti-lateral-flexion builder.", "strength", "core", listOf("glutes", "forearms", "back"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Stir the Pot", "Assume a forearm plank with your forearms on a stability ball, then draw slow circles with the elbows in both directions while the body stays rigid. Adds instability and shoulder motion to the plank, dramatically increasing the anti-extension challenge.", "strength", "core", listOf("shoulders"), "other"),
    Seed("Power Clean", "From the floor or hang, pull the barbell explosively by extending the hips, knees and ankles, shrug hard and pull yourself under to catch the bar on the front of the shoulders in a quarter squat, then stand. The premier expression of total-body power, taught widely to athletes for speed and explosiveness. Learn technique with light loads first.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "back", "traps", "shoulders"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Hang Clean", "Start standing with the bar at mid-thigh. Dip slightly, then explosively extend the hips and pull under to catch the bar in the front rack. Removing the floor pull simplifies the movement, making it the standard entry point for learning the clean.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "traps", "shoulders"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Clean and Press", "Clean the barbell from the floor to the shoulders, then press or push press it overhead to lockout, lower and repeat. An old-time strongman staple training nearly every muscle in one lift, from the legs and back through the shoulders and arms.", "strength", "full body", listOf("shoulders", "thighs", "glutes", "triceps"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Snatch", "With a wide grip, pull the bar explosively from the floor and drop under it, catching it locked out overhead in a deep squat, then stand. The fastest lift in sport, demanding maximal power, mobility and precision. Requires coaching and light-load practice to master.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "back", "shoulders"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Power Snatch", "Snatch the bar from the floor or hang but catch it overhead in a quarter squat rather than a full squat. Emphasizes explosive triple extension with lighter mobility demands than the full snatch, ideal for athletic power development.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "shoulders", "traps"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell Thruster", "Front squat the barbell to full depth, then drive up and use the momentum to press it overhead in one fluid motion, lowering back to the shoulders as you descend into the next rep. Combines a squat and press into one brutally effective strength-conditioning movement.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "shoulders", "triceps"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Barbell High Pull", "Pull the barbell explosively from the hang or floor, extending the hips fully and continuing the pull with the elbows high until the bar reaches chest height, then lower. Trains the powerful pulling portion of the clean without the catch, building traps and explosive hips.", "strength", "full body", listOf("traps", "shoulders", "glutes"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Landmine Squat to Press", "Hold the end of a landmine barbell at your chest, squat to depth, then stand and press the bar up and away in one motion. The angled bar path is joint-friendly, making this an accessible total-body power movement.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "shoulders", "core"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Thruster", "Hold dumbbells at the shoulders, squat to depth, then drive up and press the weights overhead in one continuous motion. A high-demand conditioning exercise that hammers the legs, shoulders and lungs simultaneously.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "shoulders", "triceps"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Snatch", "With a dumbbell between your feet, hinge down, then explosively extend the hips and pull the weight in one motion to a locked-out overhead position, dropping slightly under it to catch. Builds unilateral total-body power with simpler technique than the barbell snatch.", "strength", "full body", listOf("glutes", "shoulders", "back"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Clean and Press", "Clean two dumbbells from the floor or hang to the shoulders using hip drive, then press them overhead. A total-body strength builder that doubles as conditioning at higher reps and requires no barbell setup.", "strength", "full body", listOf("shoulders", "thighs", "glutes"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Man Maker", "Holding dumbbells, perform a push-up, row each dumbbell once, jump the feet in, clean the weights to the shoulders and finish with a thruster overhead. One of the most demanding single-piece complexes in training, taxing every major muscle and the cardiovascular system.", "strength", "full body", listOf("chest", "back", "thighs", "shoulders", "core"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Devil Press", "With two dumbbells, drop into a burpee with hands on the weights, perform the push-up, then jump the feet in and swing-snatch both dumbbells directly overhead in one motion. A CrossFit conditioning favorite combining a burpee with a double dumbbell snatch.", "strength", "full body", listOf("chest", "shoulders", "glutes", "core"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Clean", "Hike the kettlebell back between the legs, then drive the hips forward and guide the bell up close to the body, rotating it around the wrist to land softly in the rack position. The gateway to all rack-position kettlebell work; a smooth clean should never bang the forearm.", "strength", "full body", listOf("glutes", "biceps", "forearms", "core"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Snatch", "Swing the kettlebell back between the legs, then explosively extend the hips and pull the bell in one motion overhead, punching through at the top so it lands softly on the forearm at lockout. The pinnacle kettlebell exercise for power and conditioning, famously tested in the 10-minute snatch test.", "strength", "full body", listOf("glutes", "shoulders", "back", "forearms"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Turkish Get-Up", "Lie on your back holding a kettlebell locked out above you. Through a precise sequence of rolling to the elbow, to the hand, bridging, sweeping the leg through and lunging up, rise to standing with the bell overhead, then reverse every step back down. Builds shoulder stability, core strength and total-body coordination like nothing else.", "strength", "full body", listOf("shoulders", "core", "glutes"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Goblet Clean", "Swing the kettlebell back between the legs and use the hip snap to pop it up, catching it by the horns at the chest in the goblet position. Links the hinge to the goblet squat and teaches force absorption.", "strength", "full body", listOf("glutes", "thighs", "core"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Clean and Jerk", "Clean the kettlebell to the rack, dip and drive it overhead with leg power, dipping again under the bell to catch it at lockout, then stand. The long-cycle clean and jerk is a core event of kettlebell sport and a monstrous conditioning tool.", "strength", "full body", listOf("shoulders", "thighs", "glutes", "triceps"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Double Kettlebell Front Squat", "Clean two kettlebells to the rack position and squat to full depth while keeping the torso tall and elbows in. The double rack load taxes the core, upper back and breathing far more than the load suggests.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "core"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Windmill", "Press a kettlebell overhead, turn the feet 45 degrees away from it, then push the hips toward the bell while lowering your free hand down the inside leg toward the floor, eyes on the bell, and return upright. Builds oblique strength, shoulder stability and hip mobility together.", "strength", "full body", listOf("core", "shoulders", "hamstrings"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Kettlebell Figure-8", "In an athletic stance, weave a kettlebell in a figure-8 pattern around and between your legs, handing it off behind each knee. Trains grip, coordination and dynamic core control while keeping the hips loaded.", "strength", "full body", listOf("core", "forearms", "glutes"), "kettlebell"),
    Seed("Burpee", "From standing, drop your hands to the floor, kick the feet back into a push-up position, perform a push-up, jump the feet back in and leap into the air with arms overhead. The classic no-equipment conditioning movement, training the whole body and cardiovascular system at once.", "reps_duration", "full body", listOf("chest", "thighs", "core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Bear Crawl", "Crawl forward on hands and feet with knees hovering just above the ground and back flat, moving opposite hand and foot together. Builds shoulder stability, core control and coordination; crawl slowly for strength or fast for conditioning.", "distance", "full body", listOf("shoulders", "core", "thighs"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Broad Jump", "From a standing position, swing the arms and jump forward as far as possible, landing softly in a squat. A pure test and builder of horizontal power for the hips and legs; reset fully between reps for quality.", "strength", "full body", listOf("glutes", "thighs", "calves"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Box Jump", "Stand facing a sturdy box, swing the arms and jump onto it, landing softly in a quarter squat, then step down. Develops explosive lower-body power and landing mechanics; step down rather than rebound-jumping to protect the Achilles.", "reps_duration", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "calves"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Sled Drag", "Attach a harness or straps to a loaded sled and walk or drag it behind you, driving through the whole foot each step. Backward drags emphasize the quads and knees; forward drags hit the posterior chain. Concentric-only loading means high work with little soreness.", "distance", "full body", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings", "calves"), "other"),
    Seed("Battle Rope Wave", "Anchor a heavy rope and grip an end in each hand. Drive alternating or simultaneous waves down the rope with powerful arm and shoulder action while maintaining an athletic stance. Delivers intense upper-body power endurance and cardio with zero impact.", "duration", "full body", listOf("shoulders", "core", "forearms"), "other"),
    Seed("Medicine Ball Slam", "Raise a medicine ball overhead, rise onto the toes, then slam it into the ground as hard as possible using the whole body, catching it on the bounce or picking it up for the next rep. A satisfying expression of total-body power and a great core and lat developer.", "strength", "full body", listOf("core", "shoulders", "lats"), "other"),
    Seed("Wall Ball", "Hold a medicine ball at the chest, squat to depth, then drive up and throw the ball to a target on the wall, catching it as you descend into the next squat. A CrossFit staple blending a squat and push press into relentless conditioning.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "shoulders", "core"), "other"),
    Seed("Tire Flip", "Squat down and wedge your hands under a large tire, drive it up with the legs and hips, then push it over as it passes vertical. A strongman classic building total-body power; keep the back flat and drive from the legs, never curling with the arms alone.", "strength", "full body", listOf("glutes", "back", "thighs", "biceps"), "other"),
    Seed("Sandbag Carry", "Bear-hug or shoulder a heavy sandbag and carry it for distance or time. The shifting, awkward load forces continuous core and grip adjustments, building strength that transfers directly to real-world lifting and carrying.", "distance", "full body", listOf("core", "forearms", "back"), "other"),
    Seed("Smith Machine Inverted Row", "Set the Smith bar at waist height and hang beneath it with a straight body, heels on the floor. Pull the chest to the bar and lower slowly. The adjustable bar height makes scaling this horizontal pull precise and easy.", "strength", "back", listOf("biceps", "core"), "smith machine"),
    Seed("Cable Reverse Fly (High Pulley)", "From a tall kneeling or standing position, cross-grip two high cables and pull the arms out and down in a reverse-fly arc, squeezing the rear delts and mid-back. The high angle stretches the rear delts fully between reps.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("rhomboids", "traps"), "cable"),
    Seed("Trap Bar Deadlift", "Stand inside a hex/trap bar and grip the neutral handles at your sides. Drive through the floor to stand tall, then lower under control. The centered load and neutral grip make it more quad-dominant and lower-back friendly than a straight-bar deadlift, ideal for athletes and beginners.", "strength", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "back", "forearms"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Jefferson Squat", "Straddle a barbell with one foot in front and one behind, grip it with a mixed grip and stand up, keeping the torso vertical. An old-time lift that trains the legs and core asymmetrically, building rotational stability; alternate stances between sets.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "core"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Resistance Band Squat", "Stand on a loop band and hold the top at your shoulders, then squat to depth and stand against the increasing band tension. The accommodating resistance is lightest in the deep position and heaviest at lockout, matching the strength curve and sparing the joints.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("glutes"), "band"),
    Seed("Resistance Band Deadlift", "Stand on the middle of a heavy loop band and grip both ends. Hinge and drive to standing against the band, which pulls hardest at the top where you are strongest. A convenient hinge-pattern loader for home training and warm-ups.", "strength", "hamstrings", listOf("glutes", "back"), "band"),
    Seed("Resistance Band Row", "Anchor a band at chest height or around your feet while seated, and row the handles to your torso, squeezing the shoulder blades. Constant elastic tension and easy setup make this the go-to horizontal pull for home and travel training.", "strength", "back", listOf("biceps", "rear delts"), "band"),
    Seed("Glute Kickback Machine", "Position yourself in the kickback machine with one foot on the platform or pad and drive the leg back and up against resistance until the hip fully extends, squeezing the glute, then return. Provides heavy, stable isolation of the gluteus maximus one leg at a time.", "strength", "glutes", listOf("hamstrings"), "machine"),
    Seed("Pull-Over Machine", "Sit in the pullover machine with elbows on the pads and pull the bar from overhead down in an arc toward your waist, contracting the lats hard, then return to a full stretch. Isolates the lats through their longest range without biceps fatigue, a rare machine worth using where available.", "strength", "back", listOf("chest", "triceps"), "machine"),
    Seed("Standing Cable Lat Prayer Pushdown", "Face a high pulley holding a straight bar with straight arms at shoulder height. Sweep the bar down to the thighs in an arc using the lats while the torso stays tall, then return overhead. A strict lat isolation drill emphasizing the mind-muscle connection.", "strength", "back", listOf("triceps", "core"), "cable"),
    Seed("Seal Row", "Lie face down on an elevated flat bench with a barbell hanging beneath you. Row the bar to the underside of the bench, squeezing the mid-back, and lower to a dead hang. The fully supported chest makes cheating impossible, providing the strictest heavy row available.", "strength", "back", listOf("biceps", "rear delts"), "barbell"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Around the World", "Stand holding light dumbbells at your thighs with palms forward and raise them in a wide continuous arc out to the sides and all the way overhead, then reverse. Sweeps the deltoids through their full arc of motion, blending lateral and front raise work.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("chest", "traps"), "dumbbell"),
    Seed("Cable Y-Raise", "From a low dual pulley, raise the crossed handles up and out into a Y position overhead with straight arms, then lower. Strengthens the lower traps and deltoids in the overhead pattern, improving shoulder health and overhead pressing mechanics.", "strength", "shoulders", listOf("traps", "rhomboids"), "cable"),
    Seed("Reverse Nordic Curl", "Kneel upright with the ankles anchored or feet flat behind you. Keeping the hips extended and body straight from knees to head, lean back as far as controllable using the quads, then pull back up. A bodyweight quad stretch-strengthener mirroring the Nordic hamstring curl.", "strength", "thighs", listOf("core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Copenhagen Plank", "Assume a side plank with your top foot or knee resting on a bench and the bottom leg hovering, holding the body straight. Fiercely strengthens the adductors and lateral core, and is widely used to prevent groin injuries in field-sport athletes.", "duration", "core", listOf("thighs"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Outdoor Run", "Run outdoors at a steady conversational pace or in structured intervals, landing lightly with a slight forward lean and relaxed shoulders. The most accessible cardio there is, building aerobic capacity, leg endurance and bone density; increase weekly distance gradually to avoid overuse injuries.", "distance", "full body", listOf("thighs", "calves", "glutes"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Open Swim", "Swim continuous laps or open-water distance using freestyle or your preferred stroke, breathing rhythmically and pulling with long, relaxed strokes. A zero-impact full-body conditioner that builds the lats, shoulders and lungs while sparing the joints entirely.", "distance", "full body", listOf("lats", "shoulders", "core"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Outdoor Cycling", "Ride a bicycle over a set route or distance, maintaining a smooth cadence around 80-90 rpm and shifting gears to keep effort steady over hills. Builds quad, glute and calf endurance alongside aerobic fitness with minimal joint impact.", "distance", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "other"),
    Seed("Hike", "Walk trails or hills over a planned distance carrying a light pack, keeping a steady sustainable pace on climbs and controlled steps on descents. Long low-intensity work that builds leg endurance, foot and ankle resilience and aerobic base while being easy to recover from.", "distance", "full body", listOf("thighs", "calves", "glutes"), "body weight"),
    Seed("Treadmill Run", "Run on a treadmill at a chosen speed and incline, striking mid-foot beneath the hips and avoiding holding the rails. The belt makes pace precise and repeatable, ideal for timed distance sessions, tempo runs and interval work in any weather.", "distance_duration", "full body", listOf("thighs", "calves", "glutes"), "machine"),
    Seed("Stationary Bike", "Set the saddle so your knee stays slightly bent at the bottom of the pedal stroke, then ride at a target resistance and cadence for a set time or distance. A joint-friendly cardio staple, perfect for steady-state aerobic work, hard intervals or active recovery.", "distance_duration", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "machine"),
    Seed("Rowing Machine", "Drive with the legs first, then swing the torso back and finish by pulling the handle to the lower ribs; reverse the sequence on the recovery. The erg trains nearly every muscle while building serious aerobic and anaerobic capacity; track pace per 500 meters over a set time or distance.", "distance_duration", "full body", listOf("back", "thighs", "glutes", "core"), "machine"),
    Seed("Stair Climber", "Step continuously on the rotating stairs with a tall posture and a full foot placement each step, using the rails only for balance. Relentless low-impact conditioning for the glutes, quads and calves that doubles as serious cardiovascular work.", "distance_duration", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "calves"), "machine"),
    Seed("Elliptical Trainer", "Move through the machine's gliding stride at a chosen resistance and incline, driving through the whole foot and using the handles for an upper-body contribution. Smooth, zero-impact cardio that spares the knees while training the legs and lungs for time or distance.", "distance_duration", "full body", listOf("thighs", "glutes", "calves"), "machine"),
    Seed("Dumbbell Walking Lunge", "Hold dumbbells at your sides and lunge forward, lowering the rear knee toward the floor, then bring the back foot through into the next stride and continue walking. Loads the quads and glutes step after step over a set distance while grip and posture work overtime.", "reps_distance", "thighs", listOf("glutes", "hamstrings", "forearms"), "dumbbell"),
)
